From: Codex <noreply@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] glmark2: select X5 Vivante userspace in non-login shells

The vendor EGL/GLES libraries live in /usr/hobot/lib. Login shells prepend
that directory from hobot-environment.sh, but automated and non-login shells
do not. In that environment GLVND selects Mesa, which tries to load a missing
vs-drm_dri.so and silently falls back to llvmpipe.

Make the sample self-contained by prepending the vendor directory, resolving
its own data path, propagating failures, and accepting additional glmark2
arguments for unattended/off-screen regression runs.
---
 chip_base_test/11_gpu_3d_test/glmark2/run.sh | 14 +++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/chip_base_test/11_gpu_3d_test/glmark2/run.sh b/chip_base_test/11_gpu_3d_test/glmark2/run.sh
index 1111111..2222222 100755
--- a/chip_base_test/11_gpu_3d_test/glmark2/run.sh
+++ b/chip_base_test/11_gpu_3d_test/glmark2/run.sh
@@ -1,6 +1,15 @@
 #!/bin/bash
+set -e
 
-#insmod display module related drivers
+script_dir=$(CDPATH= cd -- "$(dirname -- "$0")" && pwd)
+cd "$script_dir"
+
+# The X5 Vivante EGL/GLES stack is installed outside the distro GLVND path.
+# Keep it first even for non-login shells (SSH, CI and systemd launchers), or
+# Mesa will look for a non-existent vs-drm_dri.so and fall back to llvmpipe.
+export LD_LIBRARY_PATH="/usr/hobot/lib${LD_LIBRARY_PATH:+:$LD_LIBRARY_PATH}"
+
+# Load display-related drivers. modprobe is idempotent for already loaded ones.
 modprobe panel-jc-050hd134
 modprobe galcore
 modprobe vio_n2d
@@ -9,5 +18,4 @@ modprobe lontium_lt8618
 modprobe vs-x5-syscon-bridge
 modprobe vs_drm
 
-#run glmark2
-./bin/glmark2 --data-path ./data
+exec ./bin/glmark2 --data-path ./data "$@"
